-- **Transport unavailable before egress.** A worker line `transport unavailable (pre-egress, <scope>): <reason>` means the peer did not run and no document content reached the provider; report that lens as not run with the reason. Scope `shared` (Node, `npx`, or the npm fetch of acpx) fails every route the same way, so no other route can replace it. Scope `route` (that route's CLI is missing, an acpx config file replaces its launch command, or the adapter rejected the model, with the available models listed) affects only that route. A rejected model follows the refused-model item below; any other replacement follows Step 1's new resolution, sanction, and disclosure rule.
